CHAPTER.VERS:
The watchmen who go about the city found me; [To whom I said], Did you

          {+}
         see him whom my soul loves?

I adjure you

          {+}
        , O daughters of Jerusalem, By the roes, or by the hinds of the field, That you

          {+}
         do not stir up, nor awake [my] love, Until he pleases.

Go forth, O you

          {+}
         daughters of Zion, and look at King Solomon, With the crown with which his mother has crowned him In the day of his espousals, And in the day of the gladness of his heart.
